WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.380
Touch and pain enter the cord by the same root.

2
00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:09.260
How can one cut remove touch on one side, pain on the other?

3
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.820
Picture a slice through the cord, back at the top.

4
00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:15.420
Touch runs in blue, pain in red.

5
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.240
The blue line carries fine touch, vibration and position sense.

6
00:00:21.283 --> 00:00:25.743
Its main branch climbs on its own side, with no synapse until the medulla.

7
00:00:26.643 --> 00:00:28.623
Other branches synapse in the dorsal horn.

8
00:00:29.616 --> 00:00:33.096
There, a second axon crosses and climbs to the thalamus.

9
00:00:33.956 --> 00:00:36.676
A thalamic neuron relays the signal to cortex.

10
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:39.810
So the blue line crosses in the medulla.

11
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.860
The red line carries pain and temperature.

12
00:00:43.983 --> 00:00:48.143
Its sensory axon synapses in the dorsal horn, near where it entered.

13
00:00:49.183 --> 00:00:53.643
The next axon crosses within a segment or two, and climbs the opposite side.

14
00:00:54.633 --> 00:00:57.093
So the red line crosses in the spinal cord.

15
00:00:58.083 --> 00:01:03.183
Now cut the right half of the cord at the tenth thoracic segment, Which side loses

16
00:01:03.183 --> 00:01:04.683
touch, and which loses pain?

17
00:01:10.716 --> 00:01:14.516
Fine touch, vibration and position sense are lost on the right.

18
00:01:15.376 --> 00:01:16.916
The blue line has not crossed yet.

19
00:01:17.866 --> 00:01:19.486
Pain is lost on the left.

20
00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:23.506
The red fibres in the right half have already crossed from the left.

21
00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:29.980
Now look closer. Follow one left pain fibre entering one segment below the cut.

22
00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:35.650
In this simple example, its pathway reaches the other side a segment or two higher.

23
00:01:36.633 --> 00:01:38.433
Crossing at the cut, it is lost.

24
00:01:39.493 --> 00:01:40.993
Crossing above the cut, it is spared.

25
00:01:44.033 --> 00:01:47.973
So the pain loss on the left begins one or two segments below the cut.

26
00:01:48.966 --> 00:01:53.086
On the right, at the cut itself, a narrow band can lose sensation too.

27
00:01:53.966 --> 00:01:58.266
The cut damages the sensory fibres entering there, and the dorsal horn they reach.

28
00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:04.380
Fine touch lost on one side and pain on the other is the core of the Brown-Séquard

29
00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:05.380
pattern.

30
00:02:05.833 --> 00:02:10.793
Run it backwards. Pain is lost in the right leg, vibration in the left.

31
00:02:10.793 --> 00:02:12.853
Which half of the cord is cut?

32
00:02:18.783 --> 00:02:23.763
The left half. Vibration rides the blue line, which stays on its own side.

33
00:02:24.733 --> 00:02:28.553
For these two routes, where a line crosses tells you where the damage is.
